eval-anything

Terminal-Bench 2.1 comes from harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2-1.
DeepSWE v1.1 comes from datacurve-ai/deep-swe. The Mini agent configuration is adapted
for EnvWeaver. Upstream PROVENANCE.md lists the projects used by individual tasks.
Claw-Eval General comes from claw-eval/claw-eval and claw-eval/Claw-Eval.
The EnvWeaver packaging and evaluation adapters in this repository are downstream
adaptations. See the license files under each eval_anything/benchmarks/<benchmark>/assets directory. The upstream source
archives, fixtures and container images retain their respective licenses.

The Terminal-Bench download digests come from the official astral-sh/uv 0.9.5
release assets and crates/uv-python/download-metadata.json at that tag.

The small Claw General supplement in eval_anything/benchmarks/claw/assets/fixtures
is the difference between data/fixtures.tar.gz at dataset revision
ca978fd82edb77d52f26f4ccf3f9684a8df84341 and the General task files in
claw-eval/claw-eval at 5680b8b11ff2ee5dd2b07b89086a29a5c5c984d7.
To reproduce it from those archives, run
uv run python -m tools.pack_claw_fixtures SOURCE.tar.gz fixtures.tar.gz NEW_DIRECTORY.

Agents’ Last Exam v1.1 comes from rdi-berkeley/agents-last-exam via the
potatoQi/agents-last-exam fork. Its source,
data and images retain their upstream licenses and access conditions.

GDPval tasks and human deliverables come from openai/gdpval. The public GPT-5
(low) submissions come from jeqcho/2025-10-16T21-42-02plus00-00_gdpval.
The generation prompts and environment inventories follow Artificial Analysis'
published GDPval-AA v2.1 methodology. See the GDPval benchmark README for links.
